### Minecraft Modding ###
# Almost nothing produced by a dev-client/server run is tracked. The ONE exception is the capture
# harness's screenshot folder under the NeoForge 26.2 client run — that is now the primary source
# for the listing automation (see the whitelist at the bottom of this file, and
# .github/workflows/modrinth-gallery.yml). art/gallery/ remains as manual overflow for hand-framed
# shots that were not produced by a `/necgallery capture` pass.
run/
!**/src/**/run/
**/src/generated/**/.cache/
repo/
!**/src/**/repo/
PROJECT_PLAN.md
/tools/__pycache__
# Stonecutter run directories (<loader>/versions/<mc>/runs/...) — never tracked.
runs/
# python caches (scripts)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# node deps (e.g. tools/gradle-mcp markdownlint)
node_modules/
/forge/versions
/neoforge/versions
/fabric/versions

# …but DO track the capture-harness gallery screenshots under the NeoForge 26.2 client run, so the
# Sync-Modrinth-gallery workflow can pick them up. Re-include each parent dir before the files — git
# will not descend into an excluded directory, so a lone `**` is not enough. This chain has to start
# all the way up at `neoforge/versions` because that whole tree is excluded above, and it has to be
# the LAST word in this file because the last matching pattern wins.
# Recipe (git docs): at each level un-ignore the dir so git descends, then re-ignore that dir's
# OTHER contents with `/*`, so ONLY the screenshots/neroeconomy/ leaf ends up tracked — every other
# run artifact (logs, options, saves, caches, the build dir, the rest of client/) stays ignored.
!/neoforge/versions/
/neoforge/versions/*
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/
/neoforge/versions/26.2/*
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/
/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/*
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/
/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/*
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/screenshots/
/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/screenshots/*
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/screenshots/neroeconomy/
!/neoforge/versions/26.2/runs/client/screenshots/neroeconomy/**
